<Item XName="UF-OFDM with Timing and Frequency Offset BER Measurement" UserName="UF-OFDM with Timing and Frequency Offset BER Measurement" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt; &#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;UF-OFDM&amp;nbsp;BER Measurement with Interference of Timing and Frequency Offset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This&amp;nbsp;example workspace&amp;nbsp;demonstrates&amp;nbsp;uncoded BER vs SNR measurements for a&amp;nbsp;universal-filtered &lt;SPAN style=&quot;WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; COLOR: rgb(34,34,34); TEXT-ALIGN: left; FONT: 16px/19px arial, sans-serif; WIDOWS: 1; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Orthogonal frequency-division multiplexing&lt;/FONT&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;(UF-OFDM) system in&amp;nbsp;AWGN (Additive White Gaussian Noise) channel when there is another UF-OFDM system treated as interference in the condition of timing and frequency offset. Performance of&amp;nbsp;UF-OFDM system is compared with that of OFDM system. The OFDM system is provided by setting FilterLength and FilterCoef to be 1. In UF-OFDM system, active subcarriers are composed of some subbands which are consisted of pilots and data. Number of subcarriers in every subband is the same. The time domain signal of every subband passed through a filter and the transmitter signal is the superposition of that. It provides the flexibility to choose a pulse shape by changing the filter that is controlled by filter coefficient and filter length. In this example the filter coefficient in Equation is gotten by chebyshev window with length 16 and Fourier transform sidelobe &lt;A name=OLE_LINK1&gt;magnitude&lt;/A&gt;&amp;nbsp;120 dB.&amp;nbsp;The different location of every subband is implemented by multiplying the time domain data with certain frequency offset.The power of every subband is normalized.&amp;nbsp;In receiver, pilots in every subband are used for channel estimation and one dimention interpolation is done for channel response of data.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In the figure of BER vs SNR, one guard means that one subcarriers is kept as guard between two subband. Interference is added by multiplied the signal of interference user with frequency offset.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Simulation Instruction&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;A name=OLE_LINK5&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;A name=OLE_LINK4&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 8pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;1.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The &apos;NumSubcarriers&apos; is the total subcarriers and the DFT size.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;2.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Set the &apos;NumSubbands&apos; parameter to define the number of subbands in the total subcarriers and &#x2018;NumSubcarriersPerSubband&#x2019; is the number of subcarriers in every subband.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;3.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Set the &apos;StarLocationSubband&apos; parameter&amp;nbsp;to define the index of the first subcarrier in every subband and the size of this parameter should be equal to the number of subband. The element of this parameter should be in the range of [-NumSubcarriers/2, NumSubcarriers/2-1].&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;4.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The&amp;nbsp;&apos;BaseFilterLength&apos; parameter&amp;nbsp;defined the length of filter without oversampling, and its new value FilterLength&amp;nbsp;should be equal to the size of &#x2018;FilterCoef&#x2019; which is given in the Equation.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;5.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The parament &apos;PilotsLocation&apos; is the relative location according to the index of first subcarrier in every subband. The range of it is in [0, NumSubcarriersPerSubband-1]. And &#x2018;PilotsSeq&#x2019; is the sequence value of pilots. The size of &#x2018;PilotsSeq&#x2019; could be bigger&amp;nbsp;than the size of &apos;PilotsLocation&apos; so that every UF-OFDM symbol can be allocated with different pilot values to&amp;nbsp;avoid the spur in the specturm. Please set &apos;PilotsEnable&apos; to &apos;YES&apos; when UFMC_Receiver is used.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK5&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;6.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Considering the unflatness of the filter in the subband, parameter &#x2018;CompensateFilterResponse&#x2019; will multiply the data and pilots in subband with filter compensated coefficients. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;7.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The normalized timing and&amp;nbsp;frequency offset is set in Parameter Tab.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;8.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The interference user can be turned on or off by the EnableInterferenceUser parameter. When off, the BER performance is pure UF-OFDM BER without any interference signal.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;9.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; In this example, the SweepSNR sweep is provided to simulate BER vs. SNR for target user with or without interference signal; The SweepTimingOffset sweep is provided to simulate&amp;nbsp;MSE vs.&amp;nbsp;Timing offset for target user with interference signal. The SweepFreqOffset sweep is provided to simulate&amp;nbsp;MSE vs.&amp;nbsp;Frequency offset for target user with interference signal. For both timing and frequency offset, we can see that UF-OFDM (with filter length 16) is more robust than OFDM-like (with filter length 1).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;A name=OLE_LINK4&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;A name=OLE_LINK3&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-bookmark: OLE_LINK4&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Arial&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;Things to Try&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 1.&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Try UF-OFDM AWGN performance with QPSK, 16QAM and 64 QAM. The reference in the workspace is QPSK.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 1.2pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; mso-add-space: auto&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 2.&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Try different time offset and frequency offset of the interference user to confirm UF-OFDM can support relaxed synchronization requirement.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 1.2pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; mso-add-space: auto&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 3.&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Try different filter and see the influence on the BER and MSE on frequency offset and time offset.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; mso-add-space: auto&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 4.&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Try different pilot density to check the pilot effect on BER performance.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 115%; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; mso-add-space: auto&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/FONT&gt;: due to large data, the data of S1 (SpectrumAnalyzerEnv) are removed in the datasets in this example.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
